### CmsEvents Service — Sample requests
###
### Idiomatic ".http" file readable by:
###   - Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+) — built-in
###   - JetBrains Rider — built-in
###   - VS Code + "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
###
### Prerequisites:
###   1. Service running per README Quick Start (http://localhost:5000)
###   2. Local dev seed users active (cms-webhook-user / readonly-user / admin-user)
###
### =============================================================
### ONE-TIME SETUP: fill in the three @*Auth variables below
### =============================================================
### The values must be Base64-encoded "<username>:<password>" strings using
### the plaintext password YOU chose when running tools/BcryptHash during setup.
### NEVER commit real credentials to the repo — leave the placeholders in place
### and either edit locally (this file is fine to modify without committing) OR
### use a .env / .rest-client.env.json for per-developer overrides.
###
### Compute the three Base64 strings (password is a GUID per spec Notes):
###
###   PowerShell:
###     $pwd = "4d2f8c9a-1b3e-4f5d-8a7c-9e6f2b3c1d40"   # replace with YOUR GUID
###     [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("cms-webhook-user:$pwd"))
###     [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("readonly-user:$pwd"))
###     [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("admin-user:$pwd"))
###
###   bash / zsh:
###     PASSWORD="4d2f8c9a-1b3e-4f5d-8a7c-9e6f2b3c1d40"   # replace with YOUR GUID
###     printf 'cms-webhook-user:%s' "$PASSWORD" | base64
###     printf 'readonly-user:%s'    "$PASSWORD" | base64
###     printf 'admin-user:%s'       "$PASSWORD" | base64
###
### Paste the three outputs into the placeholders below.
###
### Walk-through scenarios with expected DB state in samples/scenarios.md.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@webhookAuth = Basic REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_OF__cms-webhook-user_COLON_YOUR_PASSWORD
@readonlyAuth = Basic REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_OF__readonly-user_COLON_YOUR_PASSWORD
@adminAuth = Basic REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_OF__admin-user_COLON_YOUR_PASSWORD

# =============================================================
# Scenario 1: Publish a new entity
# Expected: 200, processed=1, DB has 1 row for article-1
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}
X-Correlation-ID: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-1",
    "version": 1,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T10:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Hello world", "body": "First version" }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 2: Repeat the same publish (idempotency — same version)
# Expected: 200, processed=0, skipped=1 (log reason "duplicate")
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-1",
    "version": 1,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T10:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Hello world", "body": "First version" }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 3: Publish a higher version (update)
# Expected: 200, processed=1, DB row updated to version=2 with new payload
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-1",
    "version": 2,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T11:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Hello world", "body": "Second version — edited" }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 4: Publish a lower version (superseded — skipped)
# Expected: 200, processed=0, skipped=1 (log reason "superseded_by_version")
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-1",
    "version": 1,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T09:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Old version", "body": "Should not overwrite" }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 5: Unpublish an existing entity
# Expected: 200, processed=1, DB row Status → Unpublished
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "unPublish",
    "id": "article-1",
    "version": 3,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T12:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Hello world", "body": "Second version — edited" }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 6: Orphan unpublish (spec corner case per ADR-006)
# Expected: 200, processed=1, DB has new row with Status=Unpublished
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "unPublish",
    "id": "article-never-seen",
    "version": 5,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T13:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "note": "This id was never published — spec corner case." }
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 7: Delete an existing entity (hard-delete)
# Expected: 200, processed=1, DB row removed
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "delete",
    "id": "article-1",
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T14:00:00Z"
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 8: Orphan delete (per ADR-006 revision)
# Expected: 200, skipped=1 (NOT failed — orphan delete is a no-op with Warning log)
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "delete",
    "id": "does-not-exist",
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T15:00:00Z"
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 9: Mixed batch — 1 valid + 1 validation error + 1 orphan delete
# Expected: 200, processed=1, skipped=1 (orphan delete), failed=1 (validation)
# errors[] contains the validation_error entry only
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-mixed-a",
    "version": 1,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T16:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Valid" }
  },
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-mixed-b",
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T16:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Missing version — will fail validation" }
  },
  {
    "type": "delete",
    "id": "article-that-does-not-exist",
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T16:00:00Z"
  }
]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 10: Reject unauthenticated calls
# Expected: 401 Unauthorized
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json

[]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 11: Reject wrong-role calls (readonly user calling webhook)
# Expected: 403 Forbidden
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{readonlyAuth}}

[]

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 12: List entities as normal user
# After Scenarios 1-9, expected only Published+Enabled entities
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities
Authorization: {{readonlyAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 13: List entities as admin
# Same DB state — admin sees everything including Unpublished + Disabled
# Response includes Status and IsDisabled fields
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 14: Fetch single entity by id (admin)
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 15: Fetch missing entity → 404
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/does-not-exist
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 16: Admin disables an entity (sticky flag per ADR-007)
# Expected: 200, DB row IsDisabled=1
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a/disable
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 17: Normal user cannot see disabled entity
# Expected: 404 (article-mixed-a filtered out even though it exists)
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a
Authorization: {{readonlyAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 18: Admin still sees disabled entity
# =============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 19: Verify admin disable is sticky across CMS re-publish (ADR-007)
# Publish a higher version, then observe IsDisabled is still true
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cms/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{webhookAuth}}

[
  {
    "type": "publish",
    "id": "article-mixed-a",
    "version": 2,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:00:00Z",
    "payload": { "title": "Republished — but admin disable is sticky" }
  }
]

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 20: Admin enables the entity
# Expected: 200, IsDisabled=false; normal user sees it again
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a/enable
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a
Authorization: {{readonlyAuth}}

###

# =============================================================
# Scenario 21: Non-admin cannot disable (RBAC per ADR-011)
# Expected: 403 Forbidden
# =============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/entities/article-mixed-a/disable
Authorization: {{readonlyAuth}}

###
